{"title":"2011 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Guess_the_answer)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Guess the answer)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c073f8a05257a19c2dacc368858763bb44fa3747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be a triangle with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/b/fab676152392a40e2280411f3364ea26be122018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2011, 2012,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa725c98dfe19f98809033755b801810bc298aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897470a282b6b85fa5221eacd41369b9a157f491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9da0180d6c9f9cb378cf15b3765d6ed2598bfefd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n = \\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12e13563a6df1a207dad9672dd7b73df2a96faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are the points of tangency of the incircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> to the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aaa2452d9ce4302e49ed83896ce666bd63e981c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB, BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f24d2b218b0e9ef02fc3dd6846491158adbb440.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> respectively, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1ef39be9a742204eb7347c5d32c9941e98c69d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> is a triangle with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91ae80de04ce313dba6efc4d1bbfd0881281429d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD, BE,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30be8247e2f804c432204f1a536822abfb617b63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> if it exists. What is the perimeter of the last triangle in the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/0/b60c10b4a765d25063e04b8736fa9f9bf879ba22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$( T_n )$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/6082d98ce926120437c31e06651867fa2d822cbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1509}{8} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1509}{32} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1509}{64} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1509}{128} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{1509}{256}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"503\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By constructing the bisectors of each angle and the perpendicular radii of the incircle the triangle consists of 3 kites. \n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:File2011AMC10B25.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e4/File2011AMC10B25.png/260px-File2011AMC10B25.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"260\" height=\"238\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/e/e4/File2011AMC10B25.png 1.5x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/70987852c74ed03e0d7d1d0db9d617405452d80a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=AF$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e73db3e75cd8c521bbc7b2ff9536b62a32d05f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=BE$\" width=\"83\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfb7184668b628bdc29d39c72f10f51bd2bb6ade.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE=CF$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/7760df28f3fa380941757eb80b3396a2188627f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = x, BD = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/8/f58306caa4b9f0c8b23d76403dec33ee4dd7843b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = z$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> gives three equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/965e8e5e8bd8c9aa4905bb44811f75eb0144e672.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y = a-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40a47c15c5ac2ccfb5d17cf2265b666977870cff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+z = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/ade26d39eb9af77b9fd3c94e2d11994398afb38f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+z = a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>(where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/3869a9c028169519d8478cb0208d53a0489667d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> for the first triangle.)\n</p><p>Solving gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee392e400671a942b9a1cab4c3b37ae5ee66e14a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x= \\frac{a}{2} -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"78\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/b/58b341d53a2db7b942e8d9c4ba7cd1968e624e69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{a}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a29b354af5165528ba258350bafb2933ec3481df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = \\frac{a}{2}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p>Subbing in gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40db9b6f10ff583906d78a06a76e08e04381bc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> has sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be06ba0478b543b8c4c97f16d1e688d4e9fe9718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1005, 1006, 1007$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"125\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0d8e9c5c70be5e8b812a08ce2566d0db946c608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> can easily be derived from this as the sides still differ by 1 hence the above solutions still work (now with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/5984de01a1f436ccc82505aa598a52a3700bacaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1006$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />). All additional triangles will differ by one as the solutions above differ by one so this process can be repeated indefinitely until the side lengths no longer form a triangle.\n</p><p>Subbing in gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0d8e9c5c70be5e8b812a08ce2566d0db946c608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/a/60ac389ef1f2933688aac2df07271aba080fdaa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$502, 503, 504$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/85746d1f1493a5145f5e46d2a8a07677a21580d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f35998cdd5712c9f5bd9ea35805287b9ab3f93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{501}{2}, \\frac{503}{2}, \\frac{505}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"108\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35d4698fff01484f830b3a88bd694e16f24bbfd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/7/c372abb9884b6d962ae1678b41908a93697b8fa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{499}{4}, \\frac{503}{4}, \\frac{507}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/4/8349f64aa4318484bd771a235841cb38a64828d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea9d33e1984dc10eae9d7dbcaeaee2756aa43d02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{495}{8}, \\frac{503}{8}, \\frac{511}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"108\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/0/c10b9ed42199709dcaca3a47ca36a45dc05d8ff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a11563db57c6e3448f00acbd694e01fad1b604a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{487}{16}, \\frac{503}{16}, \\frac{519}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/4803886e9f7ee473bf8ba0601a33d2458b872ed2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/9337b7bc87d63e6c59694239d2dae94c29d33b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{471}{32}, \\frac{503}{32}, \\frac{535}{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"108\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/c/09ce7108c9cb767007bb49353f9afd60f717b939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/e/21eed12de15e06a1c75ce9bae4951be9bbe25a11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{439}{64}, \\frac{503}{64}, \\frac{567}{64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/9/3a997c8d13100b2b38c175de4a901e2180774424.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e3e362547f7d5d438267b7b38da443da9f3230f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{375}{128}, \\frac{503}{128}, \\frac{631}{128}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c109803a7d8d6424aadaacac1c1ccf4c5c3414d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> would have sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/e/2ee9000aeb99aa0d07c3fcf5e582a6eb331833d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{247}{256}, \\frac{503}{256}, \\frac{759}{256}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"108\" height=\"37\" /> but these lengths do not make a \ntriangle as \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2e5f3f3a0d06e6a734543621fb7af02892f140c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{247}{256} + \\frac{503}{256} &lt; \\frac{759}{256}\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\nLikewise, you could create an equation instead of listing all the triangles to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c109803a7d8d6424aadaacac1c1ccf4c5c3414d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" />.\nThe sides of a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/5/2c53ebb5560969cb7b2de070ec4a4529135bbf75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> would be \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd07aa875e35eedbbb45fccd70fdb085e824c41a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{503}{2^{k-3}} - 1, \\frac{503}{2^{k-3}}, \\frac{503}{2^{k-3}} + 1\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"38\" />\nWe then have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/9/2b9920a8e3ee127d223e3e870d9f159e7e121231.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[503 - 2^{k-3} + 503 &gt; 503 + 2^{k-3}\\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/2635979cb9f1f962bc82b741d873a6fcebae4e5e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1006 - 2^{k-3} &gt; 503 + 2^{k-3}\\]\" width=\"198\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6f029700f30ed21a551b2d1f93a36960f925c24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[503 &gt; 2^{k-2}\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/4/3a4e819ce0c67d247883a5b6b4eae591c3f155c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9 &gt; k-2\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/401c007cc76b65082e03bb40043fa58536f10fcf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k &lt; 11\\]\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />\nHence, the first triangle which does not exist in this sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c109803a7d8d6424aadaacac1c1ccf4c5c3414d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Hence the perimeter is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174d1ce9c104ae9c4ffd610132bc78eb2b6c7ccd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{375}{128} + \\frac{503}{128} + \\frac{631}{128} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\frac{1509}{128}}\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Proceeding similarly to the first solution, we have that sides of each triangle are of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82ebeb120b02f74a8c1927635ebbb99bd31e57f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, a+1, a+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> for some number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Also, note that the perimeter of each triangle is half of the previous one. In order for the triangle to not exist, it must not satisfy the triangle inequality, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/52282353ee77ae473abc08fd5e52a10019c647ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + a + 1 &lt; a+2 \\Rightarrow a&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"208\" height=\"13\" />. Then, the perimeter would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/495ba5478f6f26f7fc84f8f79b34444198993edd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + a + 1 + a + 2 = 3a + 3 &lt; 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"243\" height=\"14\" />. So, to have a proper triangle, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1fb00c70777462a471996c72e576ebb1695e9be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3018}{2^{k}} &gt; 6 \\Rightarrow 2^k &lt; 503 \\Rightarrow 2^{k} &lt; 512$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"270\" height=\"38\" />. The first triangle to not work would have perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/7/257e3909b1427ca44a925154c63e0a3b2e8edfe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3018}{256} = \\frac{1509}{128}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />,  thus the answer is   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb01216a7b55f46b3a702fa4f0dbcb67b8d95d69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\frac{1509}{128}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"81\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This problem is a PoP(Power of Point) Bash exercise. What I did to solve this problem was look at recursive perimeters. The first ever perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/1851fbafc0a355384701dd89cce600ba4a1a3f8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 = 2011 + 2012 + 2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"17\" />. Next, by PoP, inscribing the circle gives us three new lengths, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d162eeab2730a426ffcdadce13b6cdcde4d61a61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD, BE, CF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" />. Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and homogeneously the others. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/59855511803daef7769f6d781bcd106ec905d916.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 + x_2 = 2011, x_2 + x_3 = 2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"247\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/453b1f17d4d98e5bfef91aaafe5011e2fb8ed447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 + x_3 = 2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />. If we add all these equations up and divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebce9da3fbaaee452c3f245fb2e8c546a2a88af8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 + x_2 + x_3 = \\frac{2011 + 2012 + 2013}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"282\" height=\"38\" />. Writing this with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/1851fbafc0a355384701dd89cce600ba4a1a3f8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 = 2011 + 2012 + 2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"17\" />, we get that our new perimeter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107c7c8e5a64d81ed24331e510b777b7d08345b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, is indeed equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/0906167ca58b5f443e20264e22c28df2fcd6cf5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{P_1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"39\" />. Similarly, by the same concept, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d003434ae5aed6ace69c4d19e32ded2d7cc385e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_3 = \\frac{P_1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"39\" /> and the pattern keeps going. In general, I found that for each new perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/7/2f786987db8bde0aa987a86b9a0a0845d6734bfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n = \\frac{P_1}{2^{n-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"39\" />. Now, substituting in the numerical value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56d8d9f9c02c72b2cff9ee325e9b581a9bb1df05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n = \\frac{2011 + 2012 + 2013}{2^{n-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"204\" height=\"38\" />. If you keep dividing the numerator and denominator by 2, I got that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2ae278fb45507025592058c9b3f381058ea83af9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n = \\frac{1509}{2^{n-3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />. This representation of a new perimeter in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> looks very similar to the option choices, so we're on the right path. Now, all we need to do is find out the last value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> when the sequence stops working. By the Triangular Inequality, we may be able to finish this off. Now, I won't go into depths here, but listing out terms and using the Triangular Inequality gives us:\nFirst Sequence:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e90f1cab4c2b7f7e735aca7e004bd57c35bd9d16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 &lt; 2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42f64be6447d0e4e8fa99127b92952efd5489fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 &lt; 2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91ae57fe2f522e2a497e9fbf061110f1315b4c94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3 &lt; 2011$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />.\nThe ordered triple for this set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbb585a4b03e37609d98aa1e230a246def19913e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1, x_2, x_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2f20109a834c6376de2647654a508e34efb4d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1005, 1006, 1007)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"20\" /> if you solve the PoP system of equations we got earlier. If you keep listing out terms, we can come up with the general form, and that is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/1253454ae227bb399c3f630356b1e80f8ee3c06c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 &lt; \\frac{503}{2^{n-4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/6/30667c9a3747a67b5bffb1b8736b23dbf2fb607f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 &lt; \\frac{503}{2^{n-4}} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/d/5ad631c6ec3a6e6c2e96af3b84dc7d3c63b52581.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3 &lt; \\frac{503}{2^{n-4}} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />.\nThe ordered triple for this set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbb585a4b03e37609d98aa1e230a246def19913e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1, x_2, x_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/9/9d9502b52fbfd2e09a472f73cf9b262baf3f52e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{503}{2^{n-4}}, \\frac{503}{2^{n-4}} - 1, \\frac{503}{2^{n-4}} + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"212\" height=\"38\" />. Now, if we plug in these values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/495ec646b2b1cfe91eb7fd0b408ed572aa011828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"11\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/6/ee60922c5fc5ee1941df04f838cdae71fbc29d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> into the inequalities, we see that the first two are always satisfied, but the last one is only satisfied when:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3dddc63a8c4737ce0d5f234cd84bdd0ab8f8bc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n-2} &lt; 503$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />(You will get this if you simplify the last inequality). The last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for this to be satisfied is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa17013a449147f7545eaf8c6efd44b5b9fa2034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. If we go up to our general representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2ae278fb45507025592058c9b3f381058ea83af9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n = \\frac{1509}{2^{n-3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because this is the last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />(and also the last triangle), we our final answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e687fa412d467dcdad36d6466d4accfd3bf81ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1509}{2^{7}} = \\boxed{\\frac{1509}{128}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"118\" height=\"49\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ilikemath247365\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Guess_the_answer.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Guess_the_answer)\">Solution 3 (Guess the answer)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Guess the answer)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c073f8a05257a19c2dacc368858763bb44fa3747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/3/203a21ebe5af207b55e815fc86a9e00f1b9a96ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6036$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, and the answer choices are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c59734e1d4e7dab2b23302fcb7dd203dca18b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6036(2^{-5}), 6036(2^{-7}), \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"197\" height=\"21\" />. So, we assume that the perimeter and each side legnth is roughly cut in half each iteration of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f4341a1efbe1a890de160de023b4e4b84ef444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. We also notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f48f95ec89b6c50220ecbbbb6130586135db8ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is almost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e9941b625a48e365712bf65ba68733c85b13f484.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{11}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />. The only way that the sequence will end is when the side legnths no longer satisfy the triangle inequality, and since there is a difference of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> between the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c073f8a05257a19c2dacc368858763bb44fa3747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, we take a leap of faith and guess <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/25531de2f575e05800d0adf96c711a2d3190ddfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6036(2^{-11})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"21\" />.\n~hellohi321\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Identical problem to the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22</a>.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B\">2011 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?tit